      <div type="clause" n="8.3">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IIAtr">II Atr</ref> 8.3</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="8.3" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="224" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif he cenne ofer I<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="30" target="#IIAtr_8-3.lnote.oe.30"/> scira, hæbbe I<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="31" target="#IIAtr_8-3.lnote.oe.31"/> wucena fyrst; gif he cenne ofer II<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="32" target="#IIAtr_8-3.lnote.oe.32"/> scira, hæbbe II<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="32" target="#IIAtr_8-3.lnote.oe.32"/> wucena fyrst; gyf<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IIAtr_8-3.lnote.oe.4"/> he cenna<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="33" target="#IIAtr_8-3.lnote.oe.33"/> ofer III scira<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="34" target="#IIAtr_8-3.lnote.oe.34"/>, hæbbe III wucena fyrst: ofor<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="35" target="#IIAtr_8-3.lnote.oe.35"/> eallswa fela scira swa he cenne, hæbbe swa fela<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="36" target="#IIAtr_8-3.lnote.oe.36"/> wycena<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="37" target="#IIAtr_8-3.lnote.oe.37"/> fyrst.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="8.3" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="224" ed="#liebermann"/>Si aduocet ultra unam sciram<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#IIAtr_8-3.lnote.oe.13"/>, habeat terminum unam ebdomadam; si aduocet ultra duas scyras<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#IIAtr_8-3.lnote.oe.16"/>, habeat<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#IIAtr_8-3.lnote.oe.17"/> duas septimanas de termino; si<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="18" target="#IIAtr_8-3.lnote.oe.18"/> aduocet in terciam scyram, habeat tres ebdomadas de termino: et ad quot scyras cennabit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="19" target="#IIAtr_8-3.lnote.oe.19"/>, habeat totidem septimanas de termino.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="8.3" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="60" ed="#robertson"/>Gif he cenne ofer I scira, hæbbe I wucena fyrst; gif he cenne ofer II scira, hæbbe II wucena fyrst; gyf he cenna<ptr type="editorNote" n="6" target="#IIAtr_8-3.robnote.fn.6"/> ofer III scira, hæbbe III wucena fyrst; ofor eallswa fela scira swa he cenne, hæbbe swa fela wycena fyrst.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="225" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn [Besitz]er [Gewährzug] über 1 Grafschaft hinaus erklärt, erhalte er 1 Woche Frist<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IIAtr_8-3.lnote.de.1"/>; wenn er [Gewährzug] über 2 Grafschaften hinaus erklärt, erhalte er 2 Wochen Frist; wenn er [Gewährzug] über 3 Grafschaften hinaus erklärt, erhalte er 3 Wochen Frist: über ebenso viele Grafschaften, wie er [Gewährzug] erklärt, so viele Wochen Frist erhalte er.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If [the possessor] declares [the vouching to warranty] beyond 1 shire, let him have 1 week's respite; if he declares it beyond 2 shires, let him have 2 weeks' respite; if he declares it beyond 3 shires, let him have 3 weeks' respite: for as many shires as he declares, let him have so many weeks' respite.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b"><ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IIAtr_8-3.robnote.n.1"/><pb n="61" ed="#robertson"/>If he can specify the county in which the man whom he vouches to warranty lives, he shall have a week's adjournment; if he can locate him within two counties, he shall have two weeks; if within three, he shall have three weeks—the number of weeks' adjournment granted him shall correspond to the number of counties which he names.</ab>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="369"><label>fits with</label> <ref target="clause:Forf_2">Forf 2</ref> <quote>fits nicely with the Appendix's extension of a suitor's time-limit by a week for every shire [n. Forf. 2, II Atr 8:3]</quote></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAtr_8-3.lnote.oe.13" n="13" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">224</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">scyr. <hi rend="italic">TMHk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">scyr. TMHk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAtr_8-3.lnote.oe.16" n="16" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">224</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">cyras <hi rend="italic">T</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">cyras T</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAtr_8-3.lnote.oe.17" n="17" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">224</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">term. u. ebd. Si ad u. d. sc. habeat <hi rend="italic">wiederh. R</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">term. u. ebd. Si ad u. d. sc. habeat repeated R</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAtr_8-3.lnote.oe.18" n="18" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">224</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">si — termino <hi rend="italic">überspringen TMHkBr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">si — termino skipped TMHkBr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAtr_8-3.lnote.oe.19" n="19" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">224</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ken. <hi rend="italic">T</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ken. T</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAtr_8-3.lnote.oe.30" n="30" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">224</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">an <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">an Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAtr_8-3.lnote.oe.31" n="31" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">224</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">án <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">án Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAtr_8-3.lnote.oe.32" n="32" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">224</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">twá <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">twá Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAtr_8-3.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">224</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">gif <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">gif Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAtr_8-3.lnote.oe.33" n="33" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">224</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">cenne <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">cenne Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAtr_8-3.lnote.oe.34" n="34" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">224</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">scyra <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">scyra Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAtr_8-3.lnote.oe.35" n="35" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">224</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ofer <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ofer Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAtr_8-3.lnote.oe.36" n="36" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">224</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">feala <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">feala Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAtr_8-3.lnote.oe.37" n="37" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">224</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">wuc. <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">wuc. Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IIAtr_8-3.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">155</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Ebenso wie hier die Frist (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 6e) zur Herbeiholung des Gewähren und später die des Vergeladenen zum Erscheinen vor Gericht, so wächst die Gebühr für Rettung des Gestohlenen (nach Forf 3) je nach der Zahl der dazwischen liegenden Grafschaften; <hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 4b. c; Anefang 20a</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Just as here the period (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 6e) for fetching the warrantor, and later that for the person summoned to appear in court, so the fee for recovering stolen property (according to Forf 3) increases with the number of shires lying in between; <hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 4b. c; Anefang 20a</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IIAtr_8-3.robnote.n.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">317</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Cf. <hi rend="italic">Forfang</hi> 3 Q.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IIAtr_8-3.robnote.fn.6" n="6" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">60</biblScope></bibl><label>cenna</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">cenne</hi> Ld.</seg></note>
      </div>
